---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import PageIntro from "../components/PageIntro.astro";
import { PROJECT_LINKS } from "../config";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Docs"
  description="How Servotab calibrates method to repository risk, evidence, and the requested outcome."
>
  <PageIntro
    index="01 / Docs"
    title="Method stays subordinate to the work."
    description="Servotab is a skills-only engineering method layer for Codex. It calibrates how much process a repository task receives without taking ownership away from the task, the repo, or the user."
  />

  <section class="content-band" aria-labelledby="working-model-heading">
    <div class="shell content-layout">
      <p class="section-index">Working model</p>
      <div class="content-prose">
        <h2 id="working-model-heading">One router. A bounded set of methods.</h2>
        <p>
          Ordinary work begins in natural language. Servotab first asks whether
          the task is already clear, local, and reversible. If it is, Codex should
          work directly. If the task carries material uncertainty or risk, Servotab
          selects the method that addresses that specific pressure.
        </p>

        <div class="direct-method-rail">
          <article>
            <span class="rail-label">clear / local</span>
            <h3>Stay direct</h3>
            <p>Inspect only what matters, make the coherent change, and verify the affected behavior.</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <span class="rail-label">uncertain / risky</span>
            <h3>Invoke method</h3>
            <p>Add design, planning, debugging, testing, review, isolation, delegation, or closure only where it protects the outcome.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="content-band" aria-labelledby="sequence-heading">
    <div class="shell content-layout">
      <p class="section-index">Sequence</p>
      <div class="content-prose">
        <h2 id="sequence-heading">Tab first. Response second. Receipt. Stop.</h2>
        <p>
          The motion grammar describes product behavior: intervention is small,
          causal, and finite. Servotab does not add ambient “thinking” animation
          or keep a task inside a process after the evidence has settled.
        </p>

        <div class="step-list">
          <div class="step-row">
            <span>01</span>
            <div><h3>The base already exists.</h3><p>The requested task and repository remain the primary surface.</p></div>
          </div>
          <div class="step-row">
            <span>02</span>
            <div><h3>A method attaches locally.</h3><p>A bounded technique appears where it can materially change confidence or direction.</p></div>
          </div>
          <div class="step-row">
            <span>03</span>
            <div><h3>The larger work responds.</h3><p>The plan, implementation, diagnosis, or review changes in a way proportionate to the risk.</p></div>
          </div>
          <div class="step-row">
            <span>04</span>
            <div><h3>Fresh evidence settles the state.</h3><p>A named check or observed result supports the claim, and then the method stops.</p></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="content-band content-band-ink" aria-labelledby="boundaries-heading">
    <div class="shell content-layout">
      <p class="section-index">Boundaries</p>
      <div class="content-prose">
        <h2 id="boundaries-heading">What Servotab does not claim.</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>It does not replace the user’s prompt, repository instructions, permissions, or Git decisions.</li>
          <li>It does not make every task follow one mandatory end-to-end workflow.</li>
          <li>It does not treat a green build as proof of deployment, runtime activation, or owner acceptance.</li>
          <li>It does not turn an explicit complete request into a scaffold, placeholder, or unnamed partial result.</li>
          <li>It does not make an OpenAI approval or availability claim. The public directory release is not live.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="content-band" aria-labelledby="availability-heading">
    <div class="shell content-layout">
      <p class="section-index">Availability</p>
      <div class="content-prose">
        <h2 id="availability-heading">Public release is still being prepared.</h2>
        <p>
          There is no installation button here because the OpenAI plugin directory
          listing is not yet live. Exact installation and invocation guidance will
          be documented only after the published package establishes those contracts.
        </p>
        <p>
          The preceding public source and implementation history remain inspectable in
          the <a href={PROJECT_LINKS.source}>historical project repository</a>. That
          remote does not yet contain the current Servotab plugin or website candidate;
          repository links will move to the Servotab identity when cutover is complete.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
